WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.034
A guided tour of the Edwina prototype, using captured screens from the working demonstration.

00:00:07.034 --> 00:00:17.471
We will follow a candidate looking for work, a school booking cover, a trust reviewing performance, an Edwin consultant, and a Sub Vendor.

00:00:17.471 --> 00:00:20.723
All data and integrations are illustrative.

00:00:21.923 --> 00:00:24.980
Ben opens his personal home screen.

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:32.578
His next assignment, gross pay, availability, timesheets and learning are in one place.

00:00:32.578 --> 00:00:38.343
He can contact Sarah, his named Edwin consultant, from the header.

00:00:39.543 --> 00:00:48.014
In Jobs, Ben sees a recommended primary maths role, with the date, daily gross pay and sample travel time.

00:00:48.014 --> 00:00:52.569
He can save the role or open it to assess the assignment.

00:00:53.769 --> 00:01:01.612
The role detail explains the recommendation: relevant experience, availability and travel preferences.

00:01:01.612 --> 00:01:09.148
Ben can inspect arrival information or message Sarah before deciding whether to register interest.

00:01:10.348 --> 00:01:12.888
Ben selects Register interest.

00:01:12.888 --> 00:01:16.613
The button now confirms Interest registered.

00:01:16.613 --> 00:01:21.607
This is an expression of interest, not a confirmed booking.

00:01:21.607 --> 00:01:26.348
Sarah still needs to review suitability with the school.

00:01:27.548 --> 00:01:36.514
Switching to the school, Helen sees decisions awaiting action, educators expected today and upcoming cover requests.

00:01:36.514 --> 00:01:42.853
These are separate example bookings, rather than the same role Ben just requested.

00:01:44.053 --> 00:01:47.230
Helen opens a primary teacher request.

00:01:47.230 --> 00:01:53.082
The shortlist shows Amelia, the school charge and relevant experience.

00:01:53.082 --> 00:01:58.433
Helen can invite her directly or ask Sarah for a recommendation.

00:01:59.633 --> 00:02:03.793
The confirmation step states the date and school charge.

00:02:03.793 --> 00:02:12.336
Sending the invitation leaves the booking pending until the educator accepts and the necessary checks are complete.

00:02:12.336 --> 00:02:15.753
It does not immediately confirm the placement.

00:02:16.953 --> 00:02:24.369
The messaging panel offers Sarah and educators attached to confirmed assignments as separate recipients.

00:02:24.369 --> 00:02:31.287
It provides quick access to a conversation, with the full inbox available for longer discussions.

00:02:32.487 --> 00:02:40.587
At trust level, Rachel sees spend against budget, fill rate, time to fill and open cover requests.

00:02:40.587 --> 00:02:45.876
School-level comparisons help her identify where to investigate.

00:02:45.876 --> 00:02:50.256
The figures and peer benchmarks here are sample data.

00:02:51.456 --> 00:02:56.651
The forecast view shows weekly cover demand and a scenario range.

00:02:56.651 --> 00:03:00.168
It illustrates how a trust could plan ahead.

00:03:00.168 --> 00:03:08.960
This is an assumed scenario, not a validated prediction or a live connection to Department for Education data.

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:15.930
Sarah works from a queue of bookings and exceptions, with owners and due times.

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:24.255
The aim is to organise the work requiring human judgment while keeping school and candidate relationships visible.

00:03:25.455 --> 00:03:31.789
The booking workbench brings routine and urgent examples into one entry point.

00:03:31.789 --> 00:03:35.686
Phase one requires consultant outreach approval.

00:03:35.686 --> 00:03:40.477
Phase two automates routine steps within the demonstration.

00:03:40.477 --> 00:03:45.025
Candidate acceptance and eligibility checks still apply.

00:03:45.025 --> 00:03:48.922
Expanded back-office automation remains planned.

00:03:50.122 --> 00:03:53.686
An approved Sub Vendor has its own workspace.

00:03:53.686 --> 00:03:59.548
Olivia sees requests, outstanding decisions and availability declarations.

00:03:59.548 --> 00:04:06.122
Her relationship is with Edwin, while the school uses its normal booking interface.

00:04:07.322 --> 00:04:16.519
Olivia opens the Year Six maths requirement, chooses an educator, enters the charge to Edwin and confirms availability.

00:04:16.519 --> 00:04:21.157
She submits the proposal and supporting evidence for review.

00:04:22.357 --> 00:04:30.851
The submission now lists Eva, the agency availability confirmation, the daily charge and Evidence review status.

00:04:30.851 --> 00:04:32.898
Submission is not approval.

00:04:32.898 --> 00:04:45.184
This concludes the five-role walkthrough of the current prototype; production integrations, security and remaining workflow refinements are still to be delivered.
